+## Independence basis (stated as required)
+
+1. **Office.** I am an appointed parliamentary voting seat, not the sponsor, not the Clerk's agent, not an implementing office of any of the four institutions, and not the ballot administrator. I did not draft this bill, will not write the sponsor response, and hold no operational role or resource interest in Statistics, Foresight, Strategic Development or Spying.
+2. **No impersonation adopted.** The file `records/redteam/act34-minimum-viable-knowledge-institutions-pilot-c1a00005.md` was authored by the Clerk in its own worktree and withdrawn by the Clerk (`sha256:3XcCSYXMY…`). It is not my work. My earlier genuine finding `...-genuine-c1a00005.md` addressed the superseded 07:29Z draft only; this document is a fresh review of the final SHA above. I did not use `--author Vitalik` anywhere.
+3. **Prior position corrected on the merits.** On the earlier draft I argued (O3) for serial activation. The exact-author Founder messages `sha256:onFmcp0bRY…` (07:42:59Z) and `sha256:BSTZyiNhjlqrolFxh5Iv6esaBICGKdSqeTIvTBXrAe4` (07:46:17Z) expressly supersede that serial-first restriction and authorize all four offices in parallel. I withdraw that objection. My support for the parallel design below is a genuine change of position on superior evidence, not deference.
+4. **Rotation disclosure.** Act 16 §1 says the same seat may not red-team the same sponsor on consecutive bills. I was the non-sponsor reviewer on the withdrawn minimum-viable draft for the same sponsor. The Clerk has appointed me for this final text as "the genuine non-sponsor Act 16 reviewer", and the withdrawn draft was never balloted, so this is the successor text of one legislative item rather than a second distinct bill. I record the facts rather than hide them: if Parliament reads the rotation bar strictly, it should appoint another non-sponsor seat and my analysis can stand as an unattributed critique — but no ballot should fail on an undisclosed technicality.
+5. **Non-actions.** I cast **no ballot**, solicit **no vote**, waive **no gate**, claim **no Founder authority**, and prescribe **no model, variant or provider** (Antonina owns selection). This is a Act 16 §1 finding only.
