+## O7 — Parallel all-four launch is lawful on current Founder authority, but provenance, per-office accountability and the codified record need correction; no efficacy gate has crept back in
+
+**Sources.** `sha256:onFmcp0bRY…`: "launch the FULL, broad, genuinely adaptive institutional expansion early, in parallel or with minimal administrative friction… allow parallel dispatch under accountable Executive resource budgets… avoid prelaunch efficacy and perfection gates, artificially small sample caps, duplicate committees or six-phase attestation." `sha256:BSTZyiNhj…`: "I expressly supersede the serial-first restriction… I authorize all four offices — Statistics, Foresight, Strategic Development and Spying — as genuinely adaptive agents in parallel under one enacted amendment that cites this communication. **One written Executive permit per office, each bounded and reversible**… Parliament must enact the amendment and seats must cast genuine ballots."
+
+**Conclusion on lawfulness.** Yes — a parallel all-four launch is lawful *once enacted by Parliament*, and the bill's `§2(1)` correctly implements it. I audited `§2(1)(a)–(c)`, `§2(3)`, `§4.2`, `§5` and `§2(2)`'s Foresight hash-binding for a smuggled prelaunch gate: `§2(1)(a)` is enactment/codification, `(b)` is the change-quality suite, `(c)` is a safety permit — all legitimate process gates, not efficacy/perfection gates. `§2(3)` expressly removes long-run value, mature calibration and strict-cap proof. `§4.2` is a safety review window, explicitly "not a tiny sample cap". `§5` falsifiers are post-hoc. `§4.1` is post-start. `§4.3` makes improvement compulsory after launch. **No prelaunch efficacy gate has crept back in.** I would decline the bill immediately if one did.
+
+**Three defects remain.** (a) The preamble provenance lists `fKiRF4a…`, `rzlgEqJQ…`, `hKboDl5p…`, `onFmcp0bRY…` but **omits `sha256:BSTZyiNhj…` (07:46:17Z)** — the very message that expressly authorizes parallel all-four launch *and* carries the "Economy and Judiciary still prove any model-using cost bound" condition. The controlling authority for O7 should be cited, with its conditions. (b) "No 'one permit = one office'" (`§2(1)`) is ambiguous: read literally it appears to negate the Founder's "One written Executive permit per office, each bounded and reversible" and the earlier schedule's C4 ("One permit MUST NOT activate two or more offices"). `§2(1)(c)` does say "per office", so the likely intent is only to remove serial sequencing — but the text must say so. (c) `§2(1)(a)` requires codification on `main`, yet the exact bill SHA `f11b9b4e…` is **not** on canonical `main`: integration commit `c6a2cbd8` is titled "Act 34 final bill + sponsor response + assumptions schedule" but landed only the obsolete minimum-viable files. A future reader could claim Act 34 is already codified. That is a durable record-integrity hazard, not a drafting nicety.
+
+**Fix F7 (before ballot).** (i) Add `sha256:BSTZyiNhj…` (2026-11-23T07:46:17Z) to the provenance and state that it is the express parallel four-office authorization, subject to its stated safety conditions. (ii) Replace "no 'one permit = one office'" with: "This removes serial sequencing only; each office still requires its own written, timestamped, source-attested, bounded and reversible permit with its own `start_utc`, ceilings and expiry. No single permit activates two or more offices." (iii) The ballot must bind the exact text SHA `f11b9b4e1a68b07160b94cba19c6cf8921aa98bbecfab5c37842205c57be96e7`; the Clerk must correct or expressly supersede the misleading `c6a2cbd8` delivery record so that the codified text is this bill, not the obsolete minimum-viable draft. (iv) Confirm that `§4.2` does not shorten or replace Act 32 §10's day-30 Judiciary review and 45-day expiry, and that `§6`'s no-enact-by-operator, Act 22 integrity and Antonina model-selection rules remain untouched.
+
